{
  "name": "Post-merger vendor consolidation",
  "domain": "Procurement / IT vendor management",
  "context": "Two merged subsidiaries arrive with separate tooling-vendor books \u2014 48 live contracts across eight categories, delivered as two spreadsheets that disagree on how capability is rated, overlap on vendors entered under variant names, and leave two transition-risk cells blank. The consolidated estate keeps 14-18 contracts: every category stays covered, no category runs more than three vendors, and the contracts still inside a multi-year term stay put.",
